 installed Python Playwright environment, cached dependency copies and an automatically allocated loopback port. No server or browser remains running afterward. The command prints failures and a single count. Details go to test-results.json. It covers native WebGPU startup from file://, physics/traversal/hazards, a full controller playthrough with invulnerability (no developer travel), keyboard, an emulated standard gamepad, multitouch, audio synthesis, standalone WebRTC and four official AI Hub harness cases. The continuous bot enables invulnerability to remove damage variance; it still uses normal collision, running, jumps, vines and ladders.\n\nVisuals are captured with ?renderer=webgl because this machine's software WebGPU canvas can be blank in screenshots. This optional URL parameter selects Three.js's compatibility backend; the default game and automated state tests use WebGPU.\n\nSource information and feedback are embedded in About and in ../exit-interview.json. Usage is intentionally “added on import”.\nEOF\nbash test.sh --visual\"","aggregated_output":"FAIL: continuous controller playthrough without developer travel: Page.evaluate: Error: missed vine {\"pit\":101,\"x\":100.87541961669922,\"y\":-0.003099761009216273,\"end\":[103.3047452090817,2.321580283088683,0.15]}\n    at cross (eval at evaluate (:311:30), <anonymous>:66:10)\n    at travel (eval at evaluate (:311:30), <anonymous>:96:6)\n    at scriptedExpedition (eval at evaluate (:311:30), <anonymous>:120:2)\n    at eval (eval at evaluate (:311:30), <anonymous>:1:7)\n    at UtilityScript.evaluate (<anonymous>:318:18)\n    at UtilityScript.<anonymous> (<anonymous>:1:44)\nFAIL: AI Hub 2 players / standard: no errors, dialogs, popups or sockets: p0: unhandled rejection: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'getSupportedExtensions')\nFAIL: AI Hub 2 players / server: every copy says hello: server\n41/44 checks passed; 3 failures\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
